WEBVTT

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.083
"Pledge!"

00:00:19.083 --> 00:00:22.125
"I, Koshi Rikdo,
hereby give my permission

00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:26.125
to turn Excel Saga into a sports anime!"

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.250
“Koshi Rikdo”

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:39.167
Japan!

00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:53.500
<i>That isn't love</i>

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.333
<i>Love isn't that</i>

00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:05.250
<i>I am in love, but I am not loved</i>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:09.125
<i>Definitely isn't love</i>

00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:13.167
<i>Derriere isn't love</i>

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:20.875
<i>I want to be loved,</i>
<i>but I never seek it out</i>

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:25.708
<i>I offer myself and throw my life away</i>

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:29.708
<i>Looking neither left nor right,</i>
<i>I will just earnestly</i>

00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:33.667
<i>Cheat, wheedle, interfere</i>

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:36.875
<i>And trample down and</i>
<i>kick strangers</i>

00:01:36.875 --> 00:01:39.125
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:41.042
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:41.042 --> 00:01:42.750
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>
<i>(And we get the hell out!)</i>

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.792
<i>And we get the hell out!</i>

00:01:44.792 --> 00:01:49.542
<i>Even if I slip on a banana peel</i>

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.792
<i>It is all for his sake anyway</i>

00:01:52.792 --> 00:01:57.292
<i>If anything, that is probably</i>

00:01:57.292 --> 00:02:05.125
<i>A kind of loyalty called love</i>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.417
Japan!

00:02:14.417 --> 00:02:15.708
Yes?

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:18.667
The goal of ACROSS
is the conquest of the city.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.750
However, we must
not forget that at best,

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.083
it is the first step towards the
conquest of the world.

00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:25.917
Yes, of course! I've never
even forgotten it by this much!

00:02:25.917 --> 00:02:28.917
Then Excel,
state what is most likely to be

00:02:28.917 --> 00:02:34.125
the common language of
the masses on a worldwide level.

00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:38.125
What a bit of a hard question
that jabs sharply at my brain cells!

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:42.833
In the end, would it not
be either music or sports?

00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:45.958
Yes, a brilliant answer, Hyatt.

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:48.500
I am honored to receive such praise.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.458
--What the?!
--Music and sports.

00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:52.792
She's so lucky! I want to receive
praise and feel honored too!

00:02:52.792 --> 00:02:55.792
Lately, Lord Ilpalazzo has only
been paying attention to Hatchan!

00:02:55.792 --> 00:02:58.125
Excel too! Excel too! Excel too!

00:02:58.125 --> 00:02:59.917
What is it, Lord Ilpalazzo?

00:02:59.917 --> 00:03:01.708
Do you like sports?

00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:04.917
Yes! I, Excel, have been clueless
in my brain since my student days,

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.792
but the one thing I was
really good at was sports!

00:03:06.792 --> 00:03:08.458
My best event was swimming.

00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:09.958
Then go swim.

00:03:09.958 --> 00:03:11.958
See you later!

00:03:13.667 --> 00:03:17.750
So, Lord Ilpalazzo,
what is our mission this time?

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.167
What is the most efficient way
to incite the masses?

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.500
What sport is ridiculously
popular among the modern youth?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.417
Please research that.

00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:28.625
Hail, Ilpala...

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:30.625
Are you watching, Lord Ilpalazzo?!

00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:31.583
This is freestyle!

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:32.500
Backstroke!

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.250
Butterfly!

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:33.917
Breaststroke!

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:34.708
Dog paddle!

00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:36.708
I pulled a leg muscle!

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.333
Bowling!

00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:50.292
Senior, I know little in the way
of sports, but is this a sport

00:03:50.292 --> 00:03:55.333
that is ridiculously popular
among the modern youth?

00:03:55.333 --> 00:03:58.208
It's almost sad how
nothing customers there are.

00:03:58.208 --> 00:04:00.208
This is bad! A crisis!
A management problem!

00:04:00.208 --> 00:04:02.250
Oh, well, it's okay. Don't mind it!

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.542
We can observe the enemy
character, get paid for working,

00:04:04.542 --> 00:04:06.208
and on top of that,
there are no customers!

00:04:06.208 --> 00:04:09.042
That group over there...

00:04:09.042 --> 00:04:10.458
What could it be?

00:04:10.458 --> 00:04:13.042
It looks like they are
shooting a television show.

00:04:13.042 --> 00:04:14.667
The strike that comes once every week.

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:16.917
You and I are already a spare.

00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:17.875
--If you're afraid of the gutter...

00:04:17.875 --> 00:04:19.750
--You can't eat cutlets on rice!
--If you're afraid of the gutter...

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.667
Rolling today as usual, Bowling Girls!

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:24.250
“Bowling Girls”

00:04:27.042 --> 00:04:30.333
Hello, this is the magnificent
combination of idols and bowling.

00:04:30.333 --> 00:04:31.792
The 20th century is about to end!

00:04:31.792 --> 00:04:34.375
The one and only bowling
show of our day, Bowling Girls!

00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:37.208
I am your host, the hustle boy,
Susumu Shikiri.

00:04:37.208 --> 00:04:40.167
Winging it from one situation
to another for twenty years,

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:41.667
I’m his assistant, Shinogi Sonoba!

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:42.167
--Mr. Shikiri?

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:42.375
--Yes, Ma'am?
--Mr. Shikiri?

00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:43.458
Why is the person bowling behind
us the same person all this time?

00:04:43.458 --> 00:04:45.417
--Why is the person bowling behind
us the same person all this time?

00:04:45.417 --> 00:04:46.917
Because she's a
staff member, you idiot.

00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:47.417
--Oh my.

00:04:47.417 --> 00:04:48.917
--And this week's guests are...
--Oh my.

00:04:48.917 --> 00:04:50.417
Over here!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.292
I-I'm Excel Kobayashi.

00:04:59.292 --> 00:05:00.917
I'm Mikako Hyatt.

00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:03.708
Together, we're the Excel Girls, you see?!

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:04.583
“Excel Girls”
Together, we're the Excel Girls, you see?!

00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:06.958
Why Kobayashi?! Why Mikako?!

00:05:06.958 --> 00:05:09.458
I do so hate knockoffs.

00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:12.583
Now, please listen to our song!
With your ears!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.583
Hey, hey, are they going to sing?

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:22.792
They certainly put a
lot of effort into publicity.

00:05:22.792 --> 00:05:23.333
--That isn't--

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.417
--All right, thank you very much!
--That isn't--

00:05:25.417 --> 00:05:28.000
This show has been brought to
you by each of these companies.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.458
Hey, we ain't sung it yet!

00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:35.083
Let us sing, ya old hag!
Our only good point is our youth!

00:05:36.958 --> 00:05:40.250
Please do your advertising
after you finish what you're here for.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.500
Okay.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:44.333
Now, I hear that the two
of you absolutely love bowling.

00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.292
Yes! I love it like avenging my parents!

00:05:47.292 --> 00:05:50.917
As long as I have bowling,
I can eat infinite bowls of rice!

00:05:50.917 --> 00:05:54.292
Yes, as you can see, we have
two very big dummies for guests.

00:05:54.292 --> 00:05:55.833
Oh, boy, don't you think?

00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:57.833
Never heard of a show like that.

00:05:57.833 --> 00:06:00.375
They are as local as they get.

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:04.375
I'd like to rent shoes.

00:06:04.375 --> 00:06:05.667
Okay, what size?

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.167
82 centimeters.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:10.167
Sir, you shouldn't make fun
of people like that.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.333
No one has feet like...

00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:13.292
But see, I do.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:29.167
That truck's gonna...

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.958
Strike.

00:06:37.042 --> 00:06:45.667
“Star Lane Bowl”
♪ Bowl and ling makes bowling. ♪

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:51.500
What?!

00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:01.667
Hey, hey, what the
hell are you thinking?!

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:04.125
You're in the way
in a tight space like this!

00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:06.958
I am a sportsman.

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:14.167
Here we go!

00:07:14.833 --> 00:07:15.875
Strike!

00:07:15.875 --> 00:07:17.375
Nice ecstasy!

00:07:17.375 --> 00:07:19.375
What in the world is this girl saying?

00:07:19.375 --> 00:07:21.542
Oh, Kobayashi's such an idiot!

00:07:21.542 --> 00:07:23.042
Okay, that was good!

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:26.333
We'll edit the strike in.
So don't worry about it.

00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:28.042
Man, your skills have opened my eyes

00:07:28.042 --> 00:07:29.667
to a new level of lousiness, Mikako.

00:07:29.667 --> 00:07:32.125
Well, I've never bowled before.

00:07:32.125 --> 00:07:35.417
What?! You're not
bowling-lover idol girls?!

00:07:35.417 --> 00:07:37.750
It's a barefaced lie,
more bare than a monkey's ass!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.083
Truly an idol-like duplicity!

00:07:40.083 --> 00:07:43.583
This is illuminating the ugly
truth that hides in our society.

00:07:43.583 --> 00:07:46.250
Very educational.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.583
Hey, Sir, what's your shoe size?

00:07:49.417 --> 00:07:50.750
My own shoes.

00:07:51.417 --> 00:07:53.500
My own shoes.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.750
My own shoes.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.750
My own shoes.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.917
Then, which lane would you like?

00:07:59.917 --> 00:08:01.583
All of them.

00:08:05.458 --> 00:08:08.750
Excuse me, we're in the
middle of recording right now.

00:08:20.292 --> 00:08:21.583
Strike.

00:08:21.583 --> 00:08:24.250
W-Who are you people?

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:28.042
We are the bowling ideology group,
"Ball and Stick".

00:08:28.042 --> 00:08:29.083
“Ball and Stick”

00:08:29.083 --> 00:08:31.125
“Ball and Stick”
Don't write it out!

00:08:31.125 --> 00:08:34.458
Starting now, this bowling
arena will be under our control!

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:36.708
But there are almost
no customers anyway.

00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:37.625
Shuddup!

00:08:37.625 --> 00:08:39.125
Oh, we're hostages, aren't we?

00:08:39.125 --> 00:08:39.792
--Nervous!

00:08:39.792 --> 00:08:40.208
--Excited!
--Nervous!

00:08:40.208 --> 00:08:42.083
--Excited!
--What do you want?!

00:08:42.083 --> 00:08:43.000
In recent years,

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:46.167
it's scandalous how the youth have
become apathetic about bowling!

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:51.500
So we're going to use your show
to promote the splendor of bowling!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:55.333
The king of sports
will come back once again!

00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.583
But people who
are apathetic about bowling

00:08:57.583 --> 00:09:00.000
wouldn't watch a show like
this to begin with, would they?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.625
The broadcast time is midnight too.
And the viewer ratings...

00:09:02.625 --> 00:09:04.292
You dummies! Don't provoke him!

00:09:04.292 --> 00:09:05.625
It's your fault!

00:09:05.625 --> 00:09:07.708
What's the point of faking strikes,
using these idiot idols,

00:09:07.708 --> 00:09:10.250
who can't even write the letter
"bo" of "bowling"?!

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.833
I can write "bo"!

00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:13.500
But you can't!

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.958
No! No! No! No means no!

00:09:15.958 --> 00:09:16.958
Shikiri!

00:09:16.958 --> 00:09:21.000
No! My life's too precious!
Don't take away my happiness!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.000
No!

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.500
You won't get away.

00:09:24.667 --> 00:09:26.792
No! Stop!

00:09:26.792 --> 00:09:28.458
My own ball.

00:09:38.375 --> 00:09:39.792
Strike.

00:09:39.792 --> 00:09:42.167
Change the contents of this show.

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:43.167
The title is...

00:09:43.167 --> 00:09:46.708
"A Historic First! Is It Okay For
Bowling To Be This Much Great Fun?!"

00:09:48.875 --> 00:09:51.583
Leader's having his fun and we...

00:09:51.583 --> 00:09:54.167
We've got our own fun.

00:09:54.167 --> 00:09:55.875
No, anything but that!

00:09:55.875 --> 00:09:57.542
I'm not confident about my body!

00:09:57.542 --> 00:10:00.042
Oh, we're wastefully young and pretty!

00:10:00.042 --> 00:10:01.750
What hopeless guys.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.333
Don't get carried away with
either ball or stick.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.375
No, anything but our bodies!

00:10:10.167 --> 00:10:13.833
One more time, anything but our bodies!

00:10:13.833 --> 00:10:18.125
Woohoo! We can bowl all we want!

00:10:18.125 --> 00:10:21.250
They sure can't resist anything
when it comes to bowling.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.917
Hey, you two main characters!

00:10:23.917 --> 00:10:25.583
Bring on the balls!

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:27.583
Oh, man, they're gonna make us work.

00:10:27.583 --> 00:10:29.083
Oh, dear.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.292
“Passionate!”   “Ball and Stick's”
“Bowling”   “One Track Guy”

00:10:30.292 --> 00:10:31.667
Passionate!

00:10:31.667 --> 00:10:33.625
One Track Bowling Guy!

00:10:33.625 --> 00:10:35.542
Heavy strike!

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:41.667
Listen well out there, boys and girls.

00:10:41.667 --> 00:10:43.792
Put your soul into the ball and
an abortive flower in your soul.

00:10:43.792 --> 00:10:45.583
--I'll initiate you in the soul of bowling.

00:10:45.583 --> 00:10:46.292
--Heavy! Heavy!
--I'll initiate you in the soul of bowling.

00:10:46.292 --> 00:10:47.708
--Heavy! Heavy!
--First, put your fingers gently into the ball.

00:10:47.708 --> 00:10:48.917
--Pound! Dollar, yen, peseta!
--First, put your fingers gently into the ball.

00:10:48.917 --> 00:10:50.625
--Pound! Dollar, yen, peseta!
--Got it, boys?

00:10:50.625 --> 00:10:55.458
Now, I'll show you an
example of a graceful form.

00:10:55.458 --> 00:10:58.292
With power! And yet, elegantly.

00:10:58.292 --> 00:11:02.125
My balance!
Oh, my sense of equilibrium!

00:11:03.625 --> 00:11:06.000
Beautiful shot!

00:11:07.250 --> 00:11:08.417
--Ouch! It hit my shin! My shin! Ouch!

00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:10.958
--Leader, are you all right?
--Ouch! It hit my shin! My shin! Ouch!

00:11:10.958 --> 00:11:13.500
Who interfered with my shot?!

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.667
Her.

00:11:14.667 --> 00:11:16.500
Yes, it was me.

00:11:18.542 --> 00:11:20.292
It wasn't on purpose!

00:11:20.292 --> 00:11:22.875
Stop right there, damn you!

00:11:24.625 --> 00:11:26.333
I can't stop!

00:11:26.333 --> 00:11:28.917
But stop anyway!

00:11:30.417 --> 00:11:32.208
Hey, this is getting annoying!

00:11:32.208 --> 00:11:34.208
Never mind, just stop!

00:11:36.375 --> 00:11:38.417
How long are you
gonna make us do this?!

00:11:38.417 --> 00:11:41.000
We don't know, but stop!

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:44.292
I'm getting tired of this!

00:11:44.292 --> 00:11:46.500
We're getting tired of this too!

00:11:47.167 --> 00:11:49.958
Damn, where did that girl go?

00:11:49.958 --> 00:11:52.375
We're having beef stew today, you know.

00:11:53.917 --> 00:11:57.917
Well, I wasn't really taking
care of any business, you see.

00:11:57.917 --> 00:12:01.000
I'm in trouble, I've left Hatchan behind.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.667
I feel embarrassed as a member
of ACROSS and as Hatchan's senior.

00:12:04.667 --> 00:12:06.667
It was sort of a shameful action to take.

00:12:06.667 --> 00:12:10.083
Oh, what should I...
What should I do, do?!

00:12:10.083 --> 00:12:11.917
I wanna go help her,
but I've got no weapons!

00:12:11.917 --> 00:12:13.792
And I've got no
money to pay a ransom!

00:12:13.792 --> 00:12:16.792
Think, Excel!
Agonize, Excel! Thinking time!

00:12:18.167 --> 00:12:19.625
Time's up!

00:12:19.625 --> 00:12:23.333
Conclusion: an idiot's thinking
is like taking a break!

00:12:23.333 --> 00:12:25.750
I'm sorry, Hatchan.
Excel was, Excel was...

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:27.375
Quit sniveling!

00:12:27.375 --> 00:12:29.875
That hurt! It hit my nose!

00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:31.208
Quit sniveling!

00:12:31.208 --> 00:12:32.583
I've heard your story.

00:12:32.583 --> 00:12:33.792
Where were you listening?

00:12:33.792 --> 00:12:35.958
The way you are now,
you can't win against them.

00:12:35.958 --> 00:12:38.500
Does that mean I should,
like, fight them?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.333
You need intensive training!

00:12:39.333 --> 00:12:40.875
Damn it, I've been quietly listening to you

00:12:40.875 --> 00:12:42.667
and you're just saying whatever
you want, clothes drying platform.

00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:44.042
I've got no chance at winning?!
I need intensive training?!

00:12:44.042 --> 00:12:45.208
What are you trying to say?!

00:12:45.208 --> 00:12:47.625
You want to save your friend, right?

00:12:47.625 --> 00:12:50.292
W-Well, sure, but...

00:12:50.292 --> 00:12:52.542
...they're expert bowlers
and they're scary

00:12:52.542 --> 00:12:55.375
and they have no
blood or tears or bodily fluids!

00:12:55.375 --> 00:12:57.667
That's why I've been
telling you to quit sniveling!

00:12:57.667 --> 00:12:59.083
Don't stand on the toilet.

00:12:59.083 --> 00:13:00.042
An eye for an eye!

00:13:00.042 --> 00:13:01.042
Put your pants on.

00:13:01.042 --> 00:13:02.375
Bowling for bowling!

00:13:02.375 --> 00:13:03.750
This is the women's restroom.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.167
A technique that can
counter their lethal bowling.

00:13:06.167 --> 00:13:07.667
You're standing out way too much.

00:13:07.667 --> 00:13:09.333
I'll teach you! I'll beat it into you!

00:13:09.333 --> 00:13:10.667
Intensive training with all your might!

00:13:10.667 --> 00:13:12.917
He's turning this into a sports
anime no matter what, isn't he?

00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:18.583
“Excel's Blazing Intensive Training”

00:13:19.083 --> 00:13:21.250
You bore that well, Excel.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.500
That was quick. It was six seconds.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.208
I've got nothing left to teach you now.

00:13:26.208 --> 00:13:28.875
Or rather, didn't we do nothing at all?

00:13:28.875 --> 00:13:29.792
Take this.

